    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1208">

                <pb facs="0987" n="977" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg977"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.4193/9–1249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Clubb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-12T18:00:00-04:00">September 12,
                            1949—6 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>625. British have agreed accept custody US property Mukden (Deptel 601<anchor
                        n="87" xml:id="d1208-f1"/>). If possible Ward should obtain receipts from
                    British Consul.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1208-f1" n="87" xml:id="d1208-f1-content">
                <p>Dated September 2, 3 p. m.; it reported that the British had been requested to
                    accept custody of U.S. property in Mukden but had not replied
                    (702.4193/9–249).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
